00:18:09,320 --> 00:18:11,673
You went back and fetched my hat for me.

261
00:18:15,020 --> 00:18:17,020
Maybe you're not so bad after all.

262
00:18:18,440 --> 00:18:19,270
Thanks.

263
00:18:26,180 --> 00:18:32,760
You put gum in here, you good for
nothing, little you're no ordinary mutt.

264
00:18:33,760 --> 00:18:34,590
Hey!

265
00:18:34,673 --> 00:18:35,503
Jotaro!

266
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:37,220
Jotaro!

267
00:18:37,560 --> 00:18:38,700
Are you all right?

268
00:18:45,760 --> 00:18:46,660
Good grief.

269
00:19:10,620 --> 00:19:11,760
Thank you.

270
00:19:45,320 --> 00:19:47,600
Thank you.

271
00:20:25,760 --> 00:20:27,420
Oh, sweet! Hey there!

272
00:20:27,540 --> 00:20:29,197
Is that a comic book
you're reading, little man?

273
00:20:29,280 --> 00:20:30,457
I've never seen one here.

274
00:20:30,540 --> 00:20:35,069
So Egyptians read comics just like the
rest of us you want so many doughnuts?

275
00:20:37,800 --> 00:20:39,577
Hey, mind if I see your comic book?

276
00:20:39,660 --> 00:20:42,137
If you let me, I promise I'll
be super careful with it!

277
00:20:42,220 --> 00:20:44,677
I'm a comic book artist who's
searching for inspiration.

278
00:20:44,760 --> 00:20:48,497
Nothing gets me jazzed up more than
checking out rare books and comics.

279
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:51,286
Let me borrow it and you
can use my binoculars

280
00:20:52,940 --> 00:20:57,557
What the hell peculiar the stories
about these two eerie looking brothers.

281
00:20:57,640 --> 00:20:59,405
I don't see the creator's name

282
00:21:01,880 --> 00:21:04,292
Wow, these are all such bizarre drawings.

283
00:21:04,580 --> 00:21:08,317
But this is fantastic print quality,
not to mention it's in full color.

284
00:21:08,400 --> 00:21:11,576
There once lived two brothers
who got along very well.

285
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:13,740
My name is Zenyatta.

286
00:21:13,920 --> 00:21:15,400
My name is Mondatta.

287
00:21:16,220 --> 00:21:17,637
Mondatta, the younger brother,

288
00:21:17,720 --> 00:21:21,597
was very shy and wouldn't do anything
unless Zenyatta was with him.

289
00:21:21,680 --> 00:21:23,000
He was always alone.

290
00:21:24,440 --> 00:21:27,617
One day, while his big brother
Zenyatta was away, Monday,

291
00:21:27,700 --> 00:21:30,837
Mondatta met a kind traveler
near the side of the road.

292
00:21:30,920 --> 00:21:34,880
He gave Mondatta yummy snacks
and let him use his binoculars.

293
00:21:35,240 --> 00:21:38,017
Mondatta had more fun than
he'd had in a long time.

294
00:21:38,100 --> 00:21:39,220
Oh, it's 10.30.

295
00:21:39,740 --> 00:21:42,880
But unfortunately, the very kind traveler

296
00:21:43,440 --> 00:21:47,120
was impaled on a telephone
pole and died a horrific death.

297
00:21:48,200 --> 00:21:50,024
Quite a weird comic you've got.

298
00:21:50,260 --> 00:21:53,025
Is this comic especially
popular in this place?

299
00:21:53,280 --> 00:21:55,277
If you ask me, it's really strange.

300
00:21:55,360 --> 00:21:57,540
The other pages are all blank.

301
00:21:57,920 --> 00:22:00,197
It's like they forgot to print the rest.

302
00:22:00,280 --> 00:22:01,200
Must be a dud.

303
00:22:03,180 --> 00:22:06,077
But somehow, I feel as though
I have a connection to it.

304
00:22:06,160 --> 00:22:07,689
It's totally pulled me in.

305
00:22:07,980 --> 00:22:09,437
This is gonna sound crazy,

306
00:22:09,520 --> 00:22:11,637
but would it be possible for
me to buy this book from you?

307
00:22:11,720 --> 00:22:12,880
It's not for sale.

308
00:22:13,360 --> 00:22:14,889
Are you deaf or something?

309
00:22:14,980 --> 00:22:16,800
My bro's book's not for sale.

310
00:22:17,420 --> 00:22:19,000
Now get out of my sight.

311
00:22:19,240 --> 00:22:20,657
This kid is your brother?

312
00:22:20,740 --> 00:22:22,280
I won't tell you again!

313
00:22:26,880 --> 00:22:29,937
Hey, what have I told you
about talking to strangers?

314
00:22:30,020 --> 00:22:33,377
There's lots of bad people roaming
the world these days, you know?

315
00:22:33,460 --> 00:22:34,340
Last call!

316
00:22:34,700 --> 00:22:37,360
The bus for Aswan is
getting ready to depart!

317
00:22:38,180 --> 00:22:39,010
That's us.

318
00:22:39,480 --> 00:22:41,777
They're on their way to
the hospital in Aswan to

319
00:22:41,860 --> 00:22:44,919
drop off their friend and
have his injuries treated.

320
00:22:47,660 --> 00:22:49,120
Ah, you don't say.

321
00:22:49,500 --> 00:22:53,147
If that's how it is, we'll just
have to wait for the next bus.

322
00:23:02,200 --> 00:23:05,420
I don't know.

323
00:23:26,880 --> 00:23:28,597
You and I are invincible together.

324
00:23:28,680 --> 00:23:30,017
Who the hell is in our car?

325
00:23:30,100 --> 00:23:30,930
It was me.

326
00:23:31,013 --> 00:23:31,843
Couldn't you tell?

327
00:23:31,926 --> 00:23:32,837
Jotaro, where's your school uniform?

328
00:23:32,920 --> 00:23:34,677
You're acting really weird today.

329
00:23:34,760 --> 00:23:36,397
The way you're clasping your hands.

330
00:23:36,480 --> 00:23:37,737
Then that would mean no.

331
00:23:37,820 --> 00:23:39,477
But the prediction can't be changed.

332
00:23:39,560 --> 00:23:41,089
I believe in you, brother.
